mum spanning tree of a given graph. Indeed, all spanning trees of an unweighted
 (or equally weighted) graph $G$ are minimum spanning trees, since each contain
s exactly $n-1$ equal-weight edges. Such a spanning tree can be found using eit
her DFS or BFS. Finding a minimum spanning tree is more difficult for general w
eighted graphs. But two different algorithms are presented below, both demonstr
ating the optimality of specific greedy heuristics.[] 
