Overfull \hbox (1901.74358pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 8242--8242
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Backtracking is a systematic way to run through all the poss
ible configurations of a search space. These configurations may represent all p
ossible arrangements of objects (permutations) or all possible ways of building
 a collection of them (subsets). Other common situations demand enumerating all
