Overfull \hbox (2101.243pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 11389--11389
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Recall the vertex cover problem, where we seek a small subse
t $S$ of the vertices of a given graph $G$ such that for every edge $(x, y)$ in
 $G$, at least one of $x$ or $y$ is in $S$. As we have seen, finding the minimu
m vertex cover of a graph is NP-complete. However, a very simple procedure will
 always find a cover that is at most twice as large as the optimal cover. It re
peatedly selects an uncovered edge, and picks both of its vertices for the cove
