ng that certain elements are much more popular than others. Further, queries of
ten have a sense of temporal locality, meaning elements are likely to be repeat
edly accessed in clusters instead of at fairly regular intervals. Data structur
es such as splay trees can take advantage of a skewed and clustered universe.[]
 
