[317]
Overfull \hbox (2878.24074pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 13060--13060
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Special efforts must be taken to represent very large graphs
 efficiently. However, interesting problems have been solved on graphs with mil
lions of edges and vertices. The first step is to make your data structure as l
ean as possible, by packing your adjacency matrix in a bit vector (see Section 
15.5 (page 456) or removing unnecessary pointers from your adjacency list repre
sentation. For example, in static graphs (which do not support edge insertions 
or deletions) each edge list can be replaced by a packed array of vertex identi
fiers, eliminating pointers and thus potentially saving half the space.[] 
