etation in counting the number of paths between two vertices in a graph. Let $A
$ be the adjacency matrix of a graph $G$, meaning $A[i, j]=1$ if there is an ed
ge between $i$ and $j$. Otherwise, $A[i, j]=0$. Now consider the square of this
 matrix, $A^{2}=A \times A$. If $A^{2}[i, j] \geq 1$, there must be a vertex $k
$ such that $A[i, k]=A[k, j]=1$, so $i$ to $k$ to $j$ is a path of length 2 in 
$G$. More generally, $A^{k}[i, j]$ counts the number of paths of length exactly
 $k$ between $i$ and $j$. This count includes non-simple paths, where vertices 
are repeated, such as $i$ to $k$ to $i$ to $j$.[] 
 []


