 the optimal solution point before solving it again. After sufficiently many it
erations, the optimum point of the resulting linear program matches that of the
 original integer program. As with most exponentialtime algorithms, run times f
or integer programming depend upon the difficulty of the problem instance and a
re unpredictable.\index{borrowing}\index{hardware arithmetic}\index{subroutine 
call overhead}[] 
