Overfull \hbox (1318.99527pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 13060--13060
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Linear congruential generators work the same way roulette wh
eels do. The long path of the ball around and around the wheel (captured by $a 
R_{n-1}+c$ ) ends in one of a relatively small number of bins, the choice of wh
ich is extremely sensitive to the length of the path (captured by the mod $m$-t
runcation).[] 
