Overfull \hbox (1959.49341pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 13060--13060
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Why? The higher the base, the fewer digits we need to repres
ent a number. Compare 64 decimal with 1000000 binary. Since hardware addition u
sually takes one clock cycle independent of the value of the numbers being adde
d, the best performance is achieved by using the highest supported base. The fa
ctor limiting us to base $b=\sqrt{\text { maxint }}$ is the desire to avoid ove
rflow when multiplying two of these "digits" together.[] 
 []


