computations on polynomials. A particularly useful algorithm is Horner\TS1/lmtt
/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s rule for fast polynomial evaluation. When $P(x)=\sum
_{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \cdot x^{i}$ is blindly evaluated term by term, $O\left(n^{2}\
right)$ multiplications will be performed. Much better is observing that $P(x)=
c_{0}+$ $x\left(c_{1}+x\left(c_{2}+x\left(c_{3}+\ldots\right)\right)\right.$ ),
 the evaluation of which uses only a linear number of operations.[] 
