Overfull \hbox (1649.74431pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 19588--19588
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Discussion: Median finding is an essential problem in statis
tics, where it provides a more robust notion of average than the mean. The mean
 wealth of people who have published research papers on sorting is significantl
y influenced by the presence of one William Gates [GP79], although his effect o
n the median wealth is merely to cancel out one starving graduate student.[] 
