 and median finding become expensive on large datasets because they require sev
eral passes through external memory. In data-streaming applications, the volume
 of data is often too large to store, making repeated consideration (and thus e
xact median finding) impossible. Much better is computing a small summary of th
e data for future analysis, say approximate deciles of frequency moments (where
