Overfull \hbox (1943.74345pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 19588--19588
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - Keep track of a set of permutations - Suppose we are gener
ating random permutations, but want to act only when we encounter one we have n
ever generated before. We can set up a bit vector (see Section 15.5 (page 456p)
 with $n$ ! bits, and set bit $i$ to 1 if permutation $p=\operatorname{Unrank}(
i, n)$ has already been seen. A similar technique was employed with $k$-subsets
 in the Lotto application of Section 1.8 (page 22 .[] 
