 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Gray codes were first developed Gra53 to transmit digital in
formation in a robust manner over an analog channel. By assigning the code word
s in Gray code order, the $i$ th word differs only slightly from the $(i+1)$ st
, so minor fluctuations in analog signal strength corrupt only a few bits. Gray
 codes have a particularly nice correspondence to Hamiltonian cycles on the hyp
ercube. Savage [Sav97] gives an excellent survey of Gray codes (minimum change 
orderings) for a large class of combinatorial objects, including subsets. An in
teresting new approach to $k$-subset generation based on rotating bit strings w
as developed by Ruskey and Williams RW09.[] 
