dots, a_{i-1}\right)$, for $i=2, \ldots, n$. Each distinct digit identifies a s
ubset, or block, of the partition, while the growth condition ensures that the 
blocks are sorted into a canonical order based on the smallest element in each 
block. For example, the restricted growth function $0,1,1,2,0,3,1$ defines the 
set partition $\{\{1,5\},\{2,3,7\},\{4\},\{6\}\}$.[] 
