gree ones. Consider new links (edges) being added to the graph of webpages. Und
er any realistic web generation model, it is much more likely the next link wil
l point to Google than www.algorist.com ${ }^{1}$ Selecting the next neighbor w
ith probability proportional to its degree yields graphs with power law propert
ies encountered in many real networks.[] 
