 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - Trees - Prüfer codes provide a simple way to rank and unra
nk labeled trees and thus solve all the standard generation problems (see Secti
on 17.4 (page 517). There are exactly $n^{n-2}$ labeled trees on $n$ vertices, 
and exactly that many strings of length $n-2$ on the alphabet $\{1,2, \ldots, n
\}$.[] 
