dware or software system design works correctly on all inputs. Suppose that log
ical formula $S(X)$ denotes the specified result on input variables $X=x_{1}, \
ldots, x_{n}$, while a different formula $C(X)$ denotes the Boolean logic of a 
circuit for computing $S(X)$. This circuit is correct unless there exists an $\
bar{X}$ such that $S(\bar{X}) \neq C(\bar{X})$.[] 
