 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 To exploit Menger\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s theorem
, we construct a graph $G^{\prime}$ such that any set of edge-disjoint paths in
 $G^{\prime}$ corresponds to vertex-disjoint paths in $G$. This is done by repl
acing each vertex $v_{i}$ of $G$ with two vertices $v_{i, 1}$ and $v_{i, 2}$, a
dding an edge $\left(v_{i, 1}, v_{i, 2}\right)$ between them in $G^{\prime}$. W
e also replacing every edge $(x, y) \in G$ by the edges $\left(x_{0}, y_{1}\rig
ht)$ and $\left(x_{1}, y_{0}\right)$ in $G^{\prime}$. Thus, two edge-disjoint p
aths in $G^{\prime}$ correspond to each vertex-disjoint path in $G$. As such, t
he maximum flow in $G^{\prime}$ gives twice the vertex connectivity of $G$.\ind
