 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - What if I have multiple types of material moving through t
he network? Every message sent through a telecommunications network has a speci
fic source and destination. Each destination needs to receive exactly those cal
ls sent to it, not an equal amount of communication from arbitrary places. This
 can be modeled as a multicommodity flow problem, where each call defines a dif
ferent commodity and we seek to satisfy all demands without exceeding the total
 capacity of any edge.\index{surface structures}[] 
