Overfull \hbox (2148.49286pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 19588--19588
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 The most natural tree-drawing algorithms assume rooted trees
. However, they can be used equally well with free trees, after selecting one v
ertex to serve as the root of the drawing. This faux-root can be selected arbit
rarily, or, even better, by using a center vertex of the tree. A center vertex 
minimizes the maximum distance to other vertices. This tree center can be ident
ified in linear time, by repeatedly trimming all the leaves until only the cent
er remains.[] 
