 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - Ranked embeddings - Place the root in the top center of yo
ur page, and then partition the page into the root-degree number of top-down st
rips. Deleting the root creates a set of subtrees, each of which is assigned to
 its own strip. Draw each subtree recursively, by placing its new root (the ver
tex adjacent to the old root) in the center of its strip a fixed distance down 
from the top, with a line from old root to new root. The output figure above is
 a nice ranked embedding of a balanced binary tree.[] 
