the four-color theorem, it is NP-complete to test whether a particular planar g
raph requires four colors or if three suffice. See SK86 for an exposition on th
e history of the four-color problem and the proof. An efficient algorithm to fo
ur-color a graph is presented in RSST96, which more recently has been formally 
verified Gon08.[] 
