 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Edge-coloring on graph $G$ can be converted to the problem o
f finding a vertex coloring on the line graph $L(G)$, which has a vertex of $L(
G)$ for each edge of $G$ and an edge of $L(G)$ iff the two edges of $G$ share a
 common vertex. Line graphs can be constructed in time linear to their size, an
d then any vertex-coloring code can be employed to color them. That said, it wo
uld be disappointing to go the vertex coloring route. Vizing\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\
T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s theorem is our reward for for discovering that we in fact have
 an edge-coloring problem.[] 
