 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Discussion: Steiner trees arise in network design problems, 
because the minimum Steiner tree describes how to connect a given set of sites 
using the smallest amount of wire. Analogous problems occur when designing netw
orks of water pipes, heating ducts, or communication devices. Typical Steiner t
ree problems in electronic circuit design require connecting a set of sites to 
(say) ground under constraints such as material cost and signal propagation del
ay.[] 
