panning tree problem in graphs (see Section 18.3 (page 549 ) when $T \neq V$, s
o we must select which intermediate connection points to use to minimize the co
st of the tree. In geometric Steiner tree, the hard part of the problem is defi
ning the positions of the new points we add to shorten the connections. Issues 
in Steiner tree construction include:[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (1733.74406pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 19588--19588
