test paths. Start with a tree consisting of the shortest path between two termi
nals. For each remaining terminal $t$, find the shortest path to a vertex in th
e tree and add this path to connect $t$. The quality of this heuristic depends 
upon the insertion order of the terminals, but something simple and fairly effe
