 practice using the observation that the left-most, right-most, top-most, and b
ottom-most points must all be on the convex hull. This usually gives a set of e
ither three or four distinct hull points, defining a triangle or quadrilateral.
 Any point inside this region cannot be on the convex hull, and so can be disca
