exist that map any set of $n$ points in $d$-dimensions into a $d^{\prime}=O\lef
t(\lg n / \epsilon^{2}\right)$-dimensional space such that distance to the near
est neighbor in the low-dimensional space is within $(1+\epsilon)$ times that o
f the actual nearest neighbor. Projecting the points onto $d^{\prime}$ random h
yperplanes will reliably do the trick.[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (2820.4909pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 19588--19588
 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Another idea is adding randomness when you search your data 
structure. A $k d$-tree can be efficiently searched for the cell containing the
