 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 The nearest-neighbor graph on a set $S$ of $n$ points links 
each vertex to its nearest neighbor. This graph is a subgraph of the Delaunay t
riangulation, and so can be computed in $O(n \log n)$. This is quite a bargain,
