 []\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Discussion: A fundamental problem in computational geometry 
is explicitly constructing the regions formed by the intersections of a set of 
$n$ lines. Many problems reduce to constructing and analyzing such an arrangeme
nt of a specific set of lines. Examples include:[] 
