abracadabra, and the eleventh character of the text is $x$. This pattern cannot
 possibly match from any of the first eleven starting positions of the text, an
d so the next necessary position to test is the twenty-second character. If we 
get very lucky, only $n / m$ characters need ever be tested. The Boyer-Moore al
gorithm involves two sets of jump tables in the case of a mismatch: one based o
n the pattern matched so far, the other on the text character seen in the misma
tch.[] 
